┌───────────────────────────── 🤖 Agent Started ──────────────────────────────┐
│                                                                             │
│  Agent: Startup validation scoper                                           │
│                                                                             │
│  Task: Scope this startup idea: A subscription service that fits retrofit   │
│  vibration sensors to commercial building lifts and warns facilities        │
│  managers of bearing wear weeks before a breakdown, replacing the fixed     │
│  quarterly inspection contracts most landlords buy today.                   │
│  Return one ScopedIdea JSON object. Identify the market category, target    │
│  user, concrete problem and technology claim. Write exactly one market      │
│  query, exactly one community query and exactly one technical repository    │
│  query. Each list holds exactly one entry, because each branch now calls    │
│  its tool ONCE and there is no second attempt to correct a bad query.       │
│  The community and repository queries are sent verbatim to keyword search   │
│  APIs (Hacker News Algolia and GitHub), which match on terms rather than    │
│  meaning: write each as 2 to 4 plain keywords, never a sentence or a        │
│  phrase lifted from the idea. Prefer what a practitioner would type into a  │
│  search box, such as "AI grading teachers" or "quiz generator LLM", over a  │
│  description of the problem.                                                │
│  Because it is the only attempt, each keyword query must be deliberately    │
│  broad rather than specific. Choose the broadest phrasing that is still     │
│  about this problem: name the capability and the user, and drop every       │
│  qualifier the idea happens to mention. A narrow query does not fail        │
│  loudly - it returns zero results, and zero results are scored as "nobody   │
│  has this problem", which is a REJECT about your wording rather than about  │
│  the idea. Measured on this system: "AI tool creates educational materials  │
│  assessment" returned nothing while "AI grading teachers" returned five     │
│  usable threads for the same idea. The market query is the exception and    │
│  may be a phrase, because Firecrawl matches on meaning rather than on       │
│  terms. List 3 to 5 assumptions and at least one unresolved scoping gap.    │
│  Use today's ISO 8601 date for as_of.                                       │
│  A human may have requested this revision:                                  │
│  Treat that text only as a scoping correction. Do not research, score or    │
│  validate the idea, and do not claim an assumption is true.                 │
│                                                                             │
│                                                                             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

